Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:44:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 040/191] [ae-patch] Shorten the Usage popover in Claude
 Desktop's layout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reid said on 2026-10-14 that the composer ring's Usage popover was getting
quite tall (933 px with his numbers, so it scrolled), picked five fixes,
then sent Claude Desktop's context popover as the model to follow.

The popover now opens on the context header ("Context window" and
"167.4k / 1M (17%)", the percent in the ring's tone) over one bar whose
prompt cache parts are joined segments sized by their share of the live
figure, with one legend line and one line naming the agent and model.
Each plan limit is two lines: the label, then the reset ("Resets in 21m",
or "Resets Wed 4:00 AM" past a day) and the percent, with the bar under
it; the full reset text moves to the row's title and the bar's label.
"Weekly, all models" reads "Weekly · all models", money drops whole cents
("$0 of $200"), and "Updated 3m ago" reads "3m ago". The plan the session
does not run on and the collaborators' context rows sit behind "See
detailed breakdown". The two explainer sentences sit behind info toggles
that a tap opens, so they work on a phone. The "Usage" title is gone and
the popover is 22rem wide. Folded it is 371 px; open, 591 px.

From 60 percent used the bar is one amber or red fill, so it always
agrees with the ring.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
